## Program checklist

### Arm the program

- [ ] State the protocol and this plan to the operator, then stop. Start execution only on an explicit go.
- [ ] On go, arm a durable goal with this exact text. "<The plan path, the PR ids in order, the verification rule, who merges, and the done condition.>"
- [ ] Read these from the default branch at program start. Re-read them at every tick.
  - [ ] `.cursor/rules/rigor-playbook-<execution>.mdc`
  - [ ] `.cursor/rules/rigor-mode.mdc` (dispatch, verify, writing)
  - [ ] `.cursor/rules/rigor-playbook-opening-a-pr.mdc`
  - [ ] each other playbook the program uses
- [ ] Arm a 30-minute audit tick. Use a timer subscription when the host has one. Otherwise re-check on that cadence inside the session.
- [ ] Use this tick prompt, verbatim. "Re-read the execution playbook from the repo and the armed goal. Audit the operation against both and fix drift in this tick. Probe every active lane and judge progress by side effects only. Stand down a stuck lane and dispatch its replacement now. Then send the operator a status message, whether or not anything changed, with the queue table of PR, owner, state, and head SHA, the verdicts since the last tick, what merged, open operator gates, and blockers."
- [ ] On the operator's hold or stand-down, send every owner a zero-writes order at once.

### Spawn owners

- [ ] Dispatch one owner per PR with the full lifecycle the execution playbook names.
- [ ] Follow this dependency graph. Start dependent work only after its parent merges, or base it on the parent branch when the execution playbook stacks.
  - [ ] <PR id> and <PR id> are independent and first. Both branch from `main`.
  - [ ] <PR id> after <PR id>.
- [ ] Hold the file boundaries. <PR id or class> touches only `<glob>`.
- [ ] Hold the review gate. <PR ids> change an interaction. They wait for the operator's review in chat with screenshots and a video before merge.

### PR mechanics, for every PR

- [ ] Resolve the forge once. GitHub via `gh`, or the host PR tool when the session requires it. Record any fallback. Never require `gt`.
- [ ] Open the PR ready when the host allows it. Cloud agents follow the host draft rule and say so.
- [ ] Run the repo's lint and typecheck once before the PR-facing push. Push with hooks on.
- [ ] Delete comments that narrate what the code shows. Keep a comment only for a non-obvious why.
- [ ] Triage every Bugbot and security-reviewer comment per `.cursor/rules/rigor-bugbot-triage.mdc`.
- [ ] Rebase onto current trunk before babysit and again before the merge-ready report.

### Verdict and merge, for every PR

- [ ] At the merge-ready head SHA, fan out verifiers. One gates lane. The ten live lanes from the PR's Verify, live block. The perf lane from its Verify, perf block. One audit lane that reads the diff and the receipts and distrusts the PR body.
- [ ] Clean only when every lane is `PASS`. Findings go back to the owner. A new head gets a fresh fan-out and a fresh verdict.
- [ ] <The merge or append rule from the execution playbook, with the patch-id rule from `.cursor/rules/rigor-playbook-shipping.mdc`.>

